# RP-P1 release tag hygiene (`v1.0.0`)

Whenever you commit changes in this public repository, you MUST move the stable release tag to that new HEAD before finishing.

## Required after every commit

```bash
git push origin HEAD   # if the commit is not yet on origin
git tag -f -a v1.0.0 -m "v1.0.0 — RP-P1 First Stable Research Release (points to latest release commit)"
git push --force origin v1.0.0
```

## Rules

- Tag name is always `v1.0.0` unless the user explicitly changes the release version.
- Prefer an annotated tag (`-a`).
- Force-update is required and expected (`git tag -f` + `git push --force origin v1.0.0`).
- Do not leave `v1.0.0` pointing at an older commit than `main`/HEAD after your changes.
- Do not force-push `main`/`master`; only the `v1.0.0` tag is force-moved.
- Do not invent empirical Results or unseal the target package as part of retagging.

## Verify

```bash
git rev-parse HEAD
git rev-parse v1.0.0^{}
# both SHAs must match
```
